\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. It passeth knowledge, that dear love of Thee,
\par My Saviour Jesus!  Yet this soul of mine
\par Would of Thy love, in all its breadth and length,
\par Its height and depth, and everlasting strength,
\par Know more and more.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. It passeth telling, that dear love of Thine,
\par My Saviour, Jesus! Yet these lips of mine
\par Would fain proclaim to sinners far and near
\par A love which can remove all guilty fear,
\par And love beget.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. It passeth praises, that dear love of Thine,
\par My Saviour, Jesus! Yet this heart of mine 
\par Would sing that love, so full, so rich, so free,
\par Which brings a rebel sinner, such as me,
\par Nigh unto God.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. O fill me, Saviour, Jesus, with Thy love!
\par Lead; lead me to the living fount above;
\par Thither may I, in simple faith, draw nigh,
\par And never to another fountain fly,
\par But unto Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. And then, when Jesus face I see,
\par When at His lofty throne I bow the knee,
\par Then of His love, in all its breadth and length,
\par Its height and depth, its everlasting strength.
\par My soul shall sing.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

